  "notes": "{犯|おか}す means to commit a crime, offense, or mistake. It always carries a negative connotation — the object is something wrong or undesirable.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{犯|おか}す\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{罪|つみ}→罪：03532_tsumi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{犯|おか}す: to commit a crime/sin\n- ⟦{法|ほう}→法：13620_hou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{犯|おか}す: to break the law\n- ⟦{過|あやま}ち→過ち：14376_ayamachi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{犯|おか}す: to make an error\n- ⟦ミス→ミス：00285_misu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{犯|おか}す: to make a mistake\n\nHOMOPHONES (IMPORTANT):\nThree verbs are read おかす with different kanji and meanings:\n- {犯|おか}す: to commit (a crime) — this entry\n- ⟦{侵|おか}す→侵す：19534_okasu⟧: to invade, to violate (rights, territory)\n- ⟦{冒|おか}す→冒す：19374_okasu⟧: to brave, to risk (⟦{危険|きけん}→危険：01141_kiken⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{冒|おか}す→冒す：19374_okasu⟧)",
